# Kerning opportunities for vic-sans-14.kbitx; tools/kbitx2font.py
# describes the format. A pair kerns by the bits set in both the first's
# right byte and the second's left byte.
#
# A starting point. Bits:
#   0, 1  overhangs at the top on the right, against short shapes on the
#         left (To, Va); bit 1 for T and Y against rounds
#   2, 3  open at the top on the right, against shapes open at the bottom
#         on the left (AV, LT); bit 3 for L
#   4     open above the baseline on the right, against . and ,
#   5     open at the bottom on the left, against l
#   6     does not collide with j
#   7     open at the bottom on the left, against a (exclude aw)
#
# chars       left      right
TY            ....11..  ...1..11
V             ....11..  ...1...1
W             .....1..  ...1....
FP7r          ........  ...1....
L             ........  ..1.11..
A             .......1  ....1...
'"            ....11..  ........
vwy           ..1....1  ........
acdegoqs      ......11  ........
mnpruxz       .......1  ........
.,            ...1...1  ........
lt            ........  ..1.....
j             .1......  ........
abcdefhiklmnorsuvwx ........ .1......
a             ........  1.......
vyVWY         1.......  ........
